                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "By using ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "3\\theta=2\\theta+\\theta",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " and using compound and double-angle results, prove that",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p15-q9-a-identity",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "center",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\cos3\\theta=4\\cos^3\\theta-3\\cos\\theta",
                  "display": true
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\cos3\\theta=(2\\cos^2\\theta-1)\\cos\\theta-2\\sin^2\\theta\\cos\\theta=4\\cos^3\\theta-3\\cos\\theta$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\cos(2\\theta+\\theta)\\\\&=\\cos2\\theta\\cos\\theta-\\sin2\\theta\\sin\\theta\\\\&=(2\\cos^2\\theta-1)\\cos\\theta-2\\sin^2\\theta\\cos\\theta\\\\&=2\\cos^3\\theta-\\cos\\theta-2\\cos\\theta(1-\\cos^2\\theta)\\\\&=4\\cos^3\\theta-3\\cos\\theta\\\\&=\\mathrm{RHS}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence solve $8\\cos^3\\theta-6\\cos\\theta+1=0$ in the domain $0\\leq\\theta\\leq2\\pi$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=\\frac{2\\pi}{9},\\frac{4\\pi}{9},\\frac{8\\pi}{9},\\frac{10\\pi}{9},\\frac{14\\pi}{9},\\frac{16\\pi}{9}$.",
          "worked": "Let $x=\\cos\\theta$.\n$$\\begin{align*}8x^3-6x+1&=0\\\\4x^3-3x+\\frac12&=0\\\\4\\cos^3\\theta-3\\cos\\theta+\\frac12&=0\\\\\\cos3\\theta+\\frac12&=0\\\\\\cos3\\theta&=-\\frac12.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing part a, solve over $0\\leq3\\theta\\leq6\\pi$:\n$$\\begin{align*}3\\theta&=\\frac{2\\pi}{3},\\frac{4\\pi}{3},\\frac{8\\pi}{3},\\frac{10\\pi}{3},\\frac{14\\pi}{3},\\frac{16\\pi}{3}\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{2\\pi}{9},\\frac{4\\pi}{9},\\frac{8\\pi}{9},\\frac{10\\pi}{9},\\frac{14\\pi}{9},\\frac{16\\pi}{9}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      }
    ]
